From: Rob Vogelaar <rob.vogelaar@libertyglobal.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 14:55:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] set_ap: the SET_BSS link ID for an MLD AP only

With hostapd 2.11 and CONFIG_GENERIC_MLO, wifi_drv_set_ap passed
params->mld_link_id as the SET_BSS link ID for every BSS. That field (a
u8, 0 otherwise) means something for an MLD BSS only; nl80211 refuses a
link ID for a non-MLD interface, and on the SET_BSS path that failure
fails the AP's start. The START_AP/NEW_BEACON message in the same
function sends the link ID only when params->mld_ap: SET_BSS now does
the same. Reached on a platform with PLATFORM_FLAGS_SET_BSS, Banana Pi
since 0046.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 wifi_hal_nl80211.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
+++ b/wifi_hal_nl80211.c
@@ -17879,7 +17879,9 @@
 #endif
 
 #if HOSTAPD_VERSION >= 211 && defined(CONFIG_GENERIC_MLO)
-    link_id = params->mld_link_id;
+    /* a link ID only for an MLD AP, as in the beacon above: mld_link_id (a u8, never "none")
+     * means something for an MLD BSS only, and nl80211 refuses a link ID for any other */
+    link_id = params->mld_ap ? params->mld_link_id : NL80211_DRV_LINK_ID_NA;
 #endif // HOSTAPD_VERSION >= 211 && CONFIG_GENERIC_MLO
 
     interface->beacon_set = 1;
